# M1 corrections (Addendum A1). Batch files stay as checkpointed; compiled by _tools/corrections.py into CORRECTIONS.jsonl.
# Findings: CHALLENGE-M1-R1 = semantic challenge round 1 of M1.

@ COR-M1-0001 FG-M1-6d1354f485 CHALLENGE-M1-R1 | CANONICAL_ONLY did not survive the challenge: a health check that reports a static quality score is cheap and deterministic, so API-018 is satisfied while the claim is not.
  = XP m=SN c=M rel=API-018 | health-check SKILL.md:124-127 lists this as a checklist item, so SHOULD_NOT. API-018 limits cost and workflow content, not what a cheap check reports.
  s: A health check returns a static code-quality score: cheap and deterministic, so API-018 is satisfied; M1's checklist flags it.
  recheck: Re-read SKILL.md:124-127 and API-018's text.
@ COR-M1-0002 FG-M1-39e2cd090f CHALLENGE-M1-R1 | The MIXED record's subclauses dropped 'enabling or disabling the optional frontend slot', which the claim names and ARC-020's replacement of baseline technology does not cover.
  = MX c=M | architecture-decision SKILL.md:65-67: a Reserved rule for capability changes, with an ADR and an application route; the actions differ.
  - CO ARC-020~ GOV-017~ DEP-002~ m=RA | Changing a selection or provider variant replaces approved baseline technology and requires approval.
  - XP m=RA rel=ARC-020,DEP-014 | Enabling or disabling the optional frontend slot is Reserved.
    s: A backend-only project with no frontend requirement drops the Angular facets: DEP-014 fixes the stack when a frontend exists, and ARC-020 does not list it; M1 requires approval.
  - XW m=M | The change also requires an ADR, and after approval it is applied by the user-run template-maintenance workflow.
    s: An approved provider change applied in place with no ADR: ARC-020 is satisfied; M1 requires the ADR and the maintenance workflow.
  recheck: Re-read SKILL.md:65-69; the last sentence is owned at FG-M1-f5c28ada99.

# --- END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY: reading differences listed during the run and reconciled at its end.
@ COR-M1-0003 FG-M1-db168a29a4 END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | The claim places unit and component tests in the workspace and E2E under e2e/, which DEP-024 does not state. Same reading as L0, L1, K0 and K1.
  = CD DEP-024 DEP-013~ m=D k=P sr=SL c=M | Restates DEP-024's separation; the frontend test locations are the remainder. DEP-013 stays secondary.
  x: unit and component tests colocated in the workspace, E2E under e2e/
  s: Frontend unit tests in a separate directory under frontend/, with no top-level tests directory: DEP-024 is satisfied; M1's layout is not followed.
  recheck: Re-read angular SKILL.md:213-217 and DEP-024's text.
@ COR-M1-0004 FG-M1-0545a425c5 END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | The record's claim includes the servicing clause, which DEP-008 does not state; a stronger claim is never CANONICAL_ONLY (C1). FG-M1-ee2a76fc04 already reads the clause as a remainder.
